# Nissan Primera P10 four-door saloon, 1990-1996.
#
# The car that replaced the Bluebird, built at Sunderland from September 1990
# and European Car of the Year for 1991. Its long wheelbase and short overhangs
# are the defining proportions.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Primera
#
# Dimensions 4.481 x 1.747 x 1.372 m, wheelbase 2.704 m, from the English
# Wikipedia P10 dimension box. The wheelbase is nearly 180 mm longer than the
# Bluebird 910's and is modelled as published. Mirrors take the modelled width
# to 1.947 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the P10 was located, so the objects carry
# plain colour names rather than invented marketing names: silver, red, white
# and blue. Weights silver 3, red 3, white 2, blue 2, total 10, provisional
# pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h for the 1.6, the volume fleet model; the 2.0 was quicker and
# the eGT quicker still, neither is modelled. Comfort 90/315, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 90, the same as the Rover 200 R3 and a step above the Bluebird's
# 65/280. Classes 1,2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: September 1990 intro, retires staggered 2005-2008 on
# a fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-primera-p10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-primera-p10.dae (46 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-primera-p10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the body is more angular
# than the photographed car, and the glazing is proud panels rather than the
# near-flush surface of the real car. At 128 px the long wheelbase, the low
# roof and the broad rear lamps read correctly.

obj=citycar
name=NissanPrimeraP10(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1990
intro_month=9
retire_year=2008
retire_month=6
speed=180
